-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------HOOK-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Hooks are deterministic commands that guarantee certain rules are enforced in your project.

For example, in our Conecta codebase, we may not want an agent to call the CRM API because it contains clients' personal data. A prompt alone is not enough to reliably prevent that.

Instead, we can create a hook that runs before the agent calls the CRM API. The hook blocks the request, explains why the action is not allowed, and prevents the agent from proceeding. 
